meta {
  name: Get Equipment Lab Tests
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/equipment/{{equipmentId}}/lab-tests
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns the equipment's mapped lab tests", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().data).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  The `{ id, testName, testCode }[]` lab tests mapped to an **equipment** in Site
  Admin (`EquipmentLabTest`). This is a **business** route (global JwtAuthGuard) on
  the SiteAdmin-owned Equipment module — equipment is platform-level and has no
  RLS, so a business token can read the global mapping. 404 `EQUIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`
  if the equipment is missing or soft-deleted.

  Used by the **Add Lab Adapter** form to (a) display an equipment's tests once it
  is selected, and (b) drive per-branch **auto-mapping** on create — see *Create
  Lab Adapter*.

  **Sample response — 200**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": [
      { "id": "3f1a…", "testName": "Complete Blood Count", "testCode": "CBC" },
      { "id": "9c2b…", "testName": "Lipid Profile", "testCode": "LIP" }
    ],
    "meta": { "timestamp": "2026-07-21T09:00:00.000Z" }
  }
  ```
}
